properties.description:
At step 2 of flow:release-cut, beside the changelog's assembly: the release's opening paragraph and its ### Deprecated and ### Removed sections list every entry deprecation::REGISTRY deprecates in this release, each with its What to do line, and every item this release removes (a tool removed now answers its old name with a refusal saying what to do, for this one release). Each new entry's deprecated_in is set to this release's version; tests/every_deprecation_is_announced_in_the_changelog.rs checks the assembled section. Telling the people who rely on the MCP server is owed before the release ships. Who tells Alex, and how, was decided on 2026-10-14 (dec:anthony-tells-the-mcp-users-of-a-deprecation-before-the-release-ships):
- the cutting agent drafts a short note from the release's Deprecated and Removed entries and their What to do lines;
- Anthony sends it, and the agent never does (a Gmail draft only on his request);
- the release is not tagged until he says he has told Alex;
- a release that deprecates and removes nothing owes no note. Written into AGENTS.md (the flow:release-cut bullet) on 2026-10-14 with cap:a-served-item-is-removed-only-after-a-release-that-announced-it (#751), which is the rule this step serves at the cut: that one is the mechanism in the build, this one is what the person cutting does. Planned until a cut first applies it, which is the release carrying the first deprecation. Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019Xbw6PG9mXJiU2Sb421fnq
